  "hints": [
    "Sorting makes the direction of sum changes predictable.",
    "Fix one index, then move two pointers over the remaining suffix.",
    "Record a sum when its absolute target distance improves. Increase the left pointer if too small; otherwise decrease the right pointer.",
    "Start the left pointer after the fixed index so each chosen position is different; duplicate values are allowed."
  ],
  "editorial": "Sort a copy and fix each possible first index. For the remaining suffix, start at its smallest and largest values. A sum below target can only improve by increasing the left value; a sum above target can only improve by decreasing the right value. Track the smallest absolute target distance and return immediately on an exact match. Each fixed-index pass is linear. The independent oracle enumerates all triples of distinct positions and rejects ambiguous inputs with two equally close sums.",
